+<article class="legal-page">
+  <span class="blog-tag">AI Coach</span>
+  <h1>An AI Fitness Coach That Reads Your Training and Messages You First</h1>
+  <p>Many apps sold as an “AI fitness coach” are really a chatbot with a workout theme. You can ask
+    them about training in general, but they don’t know what you did this week. The Sweats AI
+    coach is built on your own logged activity. It answers questions about your real pace,
+    distance and streaks. It messages you first when something is worth saying. And once you confirm,
+    it can set things up for you, like a challenge with a friend.</p>
+
+  <div class="blog-cta">
+    <p>Ask an AI coach about your own training and get a real answer.</p>
+    <a href="/#download" class="btn btn-primary">Get Sweats free</a>
+  </div>
+
+  <h2>What the Sweats AI coach does</h2>
+
+  <h3>1. Answers questions from your own history</h3>
+  <p>Ask <em>“How was my long run this week compared to last?”</em> and it answers from your logged
+    activity, not from general advice written for everyone. You get feedback on pacing, training load
+    and recovery based on what you actually recorded.</p>
+
+  <h3>2. Messages you first</h3>
+  <p>Most fitness apps wait for you to open them. The Sweats coach watches for real signals in your
+    training and sends you a direct message in your inbox (not a generic push notification) when:</p>
+  <ul>
+    <li><strong>Your streak is about to break.</strong> For example: <em>“Your 12-day streak is about to slip. A quick
+      15-min walk before midnight keeps it alive.”</em> It comes before you lose the streak,
+      not as a guilt trip afterwards.</li>
+    <li><strong>You’ve had a strong week.</strong> It tells you what improved, using your actual numbers.</li>
+    <li><strong>You’re behind in a duel or challenge.</strong> It gives you the real gap and the time
+      left, so you know exactly what it takes to catch up.</li>
+  </ul>
+
+  <h3>3. Sets things up once you confirm</h3>
+  <p>Say <em>“Set up a 7-day step challenge for me and Jordan”</em> and it drafts the challenge. You review
+    it, then confirm or edit it. Nothing is created until you tap confirm.</p>
+
+  <h3>4. Builds challenges people finish</h3>
+  <p>The AI Challenge Builder takes a type, a length and a fitness level and writes the title, the
+    goal, day-by-day milestones, tips and hashtags. Milestones are paced to keep people going, not a
+    flat daily number that half the group gives up on. For the reasons why, see
+    <a href="/blog/why-group-fitness-challenges-fail">why most group fitness challenges fail by day 3</a>.</p>
+
+  <h3>5. Drafts captions and replies</h3>
+  <p>After a workout you get a caption suggestion based on what you actually did: distance, pace,
+    effort and who you trained with. It works for comment replies too. You always review the draft and post it yourself.</p>
+
+  <h2>The line it won’t cross</h2>
+  <p>An AI that can draft things is useful. An AI that posts, messages other people or joins things
+    for you without asking is a risk. So the Sweats coach follows one rule: messages addressed
+    <em>to you</em> can arrive on their own, but <strong>nothing addressed to anyone else is posted,
+    created or sent until you’ve reviewed and confirmed it</strong>. We explain this design in
+    <a href="/blog/what-an-ai-fitness-coach-should-do">what an AI fitness coach should actually do</a>.</p>
+
+  <h2>How to tell a real AI coach from a chatbot</h2>
+  <p>Before you trust any app’s “AI coach” claim, ask it something only your own data could answer:</p>
+  <ul>
+    <li>“How does this week compare to last week?”</li>
+    <li>“Is my easy pace getting faster?”</li>
+    <li>“How many days have I trained this month?”</li>
+  </ul>
+  <p>A coach that knows your history will answer. A chatbot will change the subject or offer general
+    encouragement. That one test tells you most of what you need to know.</p>
+
+  <h2>Part of the app, not a separate one</h2>
+  <p>The AI coach lives inside Sweats, next to your workouts, your
+    <a href="/fitness-duels">duels with friends</a>, your weekly league and your tribes. There’s no
+    separate app, login or data export. It already has your training because that’s where
+    you log it.</p>
